+{
+  "tool": "built-in image_gen",
+  "reference_images": [],
+  "images": [
+    {
+      "file": "389-minhwa.png",
+      "prompt": "Create ONE fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. An authentic Korean minhwa folk painting on softly textured mulberry paper, with opaque bright mineral pigments and fine ink contours. Style completely governs the anatomy, perspective and composition. A broad, charmingly flat folk landscape: a gnarled pine spreads across the upper area, a magpie perches in it, and a large comically wide-eyed striped tiger with a humorous almost human expression sits beside a smaller woman enjoying coffee beneath the tree. The woman is in her early 30s, with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, rendered through folk-painted decorative marks rather than realism. Show her seated full body on a mat, lifting a little coffee cup toward her smiling face; a croissant rests nearby on a small low tray. Use stacked planes, playful discrepancies of scale, stylized rocks and pine needles, confident ornamental brushwork, vermilion, malachite green, azurite blue, ochre and ink black. Naive lively animal anatomy and serene simplified human forms, authentic humorous Korean folk charm. This must look like a handmade minhwa painting, never like a photograph with a filter, modern cartoon or cinematic scene. Generate entirely from this text, no reference images. No text, calligraphy, captions, seal marks, signatures, or watermarks."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "390-wycinanki.png",
+      "prompt": "Create ONE fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. Authentic Polish wycinanki folk paper-cut artwork, a meticulously hand-cut, symmetrical layered arrangement of brilliantly colored opaque paper on pure white. The whole composition reads as a crisp flat ornamental cutout with a strong vertical mirror axis. In the center stands a stylized front-facing full-body woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair formed from scalloped paper spirals, freckles from tiny paper dots, round tortoiseshell glasses from layered brown ring shapes, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater expressed with repeated decorative cut-paper chevrons. She enjoys coffee, holding a small coffee cup centrally with both hands near her face. A clearly recognizable golden layered-paper croissant sits immediately below the cup on a little central folk pedestal. Large mirrored roosters face inward on either side of her, their fan tails made from many colorful nested paper shapes; branching flowers, tulips, leaves and circular rosettes form an elaborate balanced symmetrical surround. Folk proportions, angular scissor cuts, beautiful negative-space perforations, stacked paper edges with extremely subtle physical relief, vivid crimson, pink, emerald, royal blue, mustard yellow and black paper. White stays visible around and through the cutout. Let the paper-cut tradition dictate every shape; no realistic human anatomy, no painted rendering, no photographic face, no illustration pretending to be a photo. Generate entirely from this text, no reference images. No letters, text, captions, signatures or watermarks."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "391-talavera.png",
+      "prompt": "Create ONE fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. A single exquisite Mexican Talavera ceramic plate fills almost the entire square, viewed directly face-on, with its complete round scalloped rim visible against a plain pale background. The artwork is authentically hand-painted in cobalt blue, golden yellow and rich green mineral glazes on creamy white tin-glazed ceramic. Broad intricate floral and leafy border bands follow the circular rim. Inside the central medallion is a large simplified decorative three-quarter bust portrait of a woman enjoying coffee: early 30s, curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. Her small raised hand holds a decorated coffee cup close to her smiling lips; a croissant is painted beside her at the bottom of the medallion. All of the woman, coffee and croissant are visibly painted ceramic ornament, flattened and shaped by confident cobalt contour strokes, botanical curls and a limited glaze palette, with hand-painted hatch marks suggesting the knit. Use auburn-brown glaze accents in the hair and tortoiseshell glasses. Glossy vitreous highlights and faint glaze pooling reveal the curved handmade ceramic surface; slight irregularity in brushwork and scalloped rim. The dominant visual experience is Talavera ceramic art and its floral rhythms, never a photo portrait transferred to a plate. No realistic photographic face, no modern vector clip art. Generate entirely from this text, no reference images. No text, captions, stamps, signatures or watermarks."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "392-kalighat.png",
+      "prompt": "Create ONE fresh text-only image, square 1024x1024. Use case: stylized-concept. An authentic Kalighat pat painting from Bengal: flowing watercolor and opaque pigment on plain warm off-white paper, emphatic sweeping black brush outlines and delicate softly graded shading within the forms. A single large simplified elegant woman is seated in a sculptural side-profile pose facing left, legs tucked to one side on a low seat, with a gracefully bending torso and long curving arm lifting a small coffee cup to her lips. Her form fills most of the square with generous undecorated paper around it. She is in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair arranged as economical rhythmic brush spirals, visible freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses drawn in profile, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater suggested by restrained dark curved knit marks. Elegant exaggerated almond-shaped eye, graceful tapered fingers, confident rounded limbs and continuous sinuous contours dictated by Kalighat painting conventions. Her free hand rests near a little saucer holding a recognizable crescent croissant beside her on the low seat. Mustard ochre, burnt sienna, ink black, muted indigo and a little warm red, restrained translucent washes and soft volume on the face, sweater and arms. The energy is entirely in the figure and expressive brush line: plain unornamented background, no scenery, no floral border. Handmade traditional watercolor on paper, never photographic anatomy, a photo with a filter, or a contemporary cartoon. Generate entirely from this text, no reference images. No text, writing, captions, signatures or watermarks."
+    }
+  ]
+}
